      "why": "pipelined_m with m=2 is the only family that can plausibly meet the strict 0.5us p99 batch latency while keeping area low. A full pipelined (m=1) design with N=14 has 16 cycles latency, which at ~100MHz is 160ns, but the burst of 32 requests means the last request arrives at cycle 31 and needs 16 more cycles, totaling ~47 cycles or ~470ns. However, pipelined_m with m=2 has ceil(14/2)+2 = 9 cycles latency. The burst of 32 requests takes 32 cycles to enter, plus 9 cycles for the last one to exit = 41 cycles. At 100MHz that is 410ns, which is under 0.5us. m=1 would be 32+16=48 cycles = 480ns, also under 0.5us but with more registers (higher area). m=2 reduces register count by ~half compared to m=1 while still meeting latency. n_iter=14 gives ~14 bits accuracy, well above the 12-bit requirement. data_width=14-16 balances accuracy and area. angle_guard=-1 to 0 and frac_guard=0-2 explore the accuracy/area trade-off. This family is the primary candidate for the Pareto front."
