  "rationale": "The spec requires 32 Msps throughput, max error <= 2^-12, and p99 batch latency <= 0.5us for a burst of 32 requests every 1us. The key challenge is the batch latency: 32 requests must all complete within 0.5us. For pipelined designs, the batch latency is approximately (32 + latency_cycles) / Fmax. To stay under 0.5us, we need (32 + L) / Fmax <= 0.5us. If Fmax is ~100MHz (10ns/cycle), then 32 + L <= 50, so L <= 18 cycles. pipelined_m with m=2 and N=14 gives L=9, total 41 cycles = 410ns, which passes. pipelined (m=1) with N=14 gives L=16, total 48 cycles = 480ns, also passes but with more area. unrolled_k cannot meet 32 Msps because its throughput is 1/ceil(N/k) per cycle, which is at most 1/5 = 0.2 results/cycle = 20 Msps at 100MHz. So unrolled_k is likely infeasible for the throughput constraint. I focus 80% of the budget on pipelined_m and pipelined, which are the viable families, and 20% on unrolled_k to confirm infeasibility. The accuracy constraint (max_abs_err <= 2^-12) requires n_iter >= 12 typically, so I set n_iter range to 12-16. data_width 12-16 balances area and accuracy. angle_guard and frac_guard are kept small to minimize area while maintaining accuracy."
